  "instructions": [
    {
      "id": 488363,
      "primary_message": "Cut tofu in half along the long side. Sandwich tofu between clean towels or paper towels and place on a baking sheet pan. Place a cutting board with something heavy on top and set aside to press out excess water.",
      "secondary_message": "3 (340 g) pkgs extra firm tofu"
    },
    {
      "id": 488364,
      "primary_message": "Wash and dry the fresh produce.",
      "secondary_message": "1 ½ medium heads cauliflower\n3 medium zucchini squash\n1 ½ small pkgs grape tomatoes\n1 ½ yellow bell peppers\n1 small bunch cilantro"
    },
    {
      "id": 488365,
      "primary_message": "Cut each cauliflower head into quarters; using a box grater, hold the stem end of the cauliflower and coarsely grate. (Alternatively, transfer cauliflower to the bowl of a food processor; pulse until rice-like in consistency.) Place in a large bowl and set aside. ",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "id": 488366,
      "primary_message": "Trim and quarter zucchini lengthwise, then cut crosswise into bite-sized pieces. Place in a medium bowl.",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "id": 488367,
      "primary_message": "Halve tomatoes lengthwise. Add to the bowl with the zucchini. ",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "id": 488368,
      "primary_message": "Trim, seed, and medium dice bell peppers. Add to the bowl.",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "id": 488369,
      "primary_message": "Preheat a large pot over medium-high heat. ",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "id": 488370,
      "primary_message": "Once the pot is hot, add oil and swirl to coat the bottom. Add chopped veggies and spices; cook, stirring occasionally, until veggies start to soften, about 4 minutes. ",
      "secondary_message": "3 tbsp virgin coconut oil\n3 tbsp curry powder\n2 tbsp coriander, ground\n1 ½ tsp salt\n¾ tsp black pepper"
    },
    {
      "id": 488371,
      "primary_message": "Meanwhile, medium dice tofu. ",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "id": 488372,
      "primary_message": "When the veggies are softened, add coconut milk, peanut butter, sugar, chili-garlic sauce, and soy sauce to the pot. Stir to combine the curry and bring to a simmer. ",
      "secondary_message": "1 ½ (398 ml) cans coconut milk\n⅓ cup natural peanut butter\n2 tbsp brown sugar\n2 tbsp chili-garlic sauce\n1 tbsp soy sauce"
    },
    {
      "id": 488373,
      "primary_message": "Once the curry is simmering, add tofu and stir to combine. Reduce heat to low and continue to cook, stirring occasionally, until veggies are tender and curry has thickened slightly, 8-10 minutes more. Remove from heat.",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "id": 488374,
      "primary_message": "While the curry is cooking, preheat a large skillet over medium-high heat.",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "id": 488375,
      "primary_message": "Once the skillet is hot, add oil and swirl to coat the bottom. Add riced cauliflower, water, and salt; cook, stirring occasionally, until cauliflower is soft, 6-7 minutes.",
      "secondary_message": "1 tbsp virgin coconut oil\n⅓ cup water\n½ tsp salt"
    },
    {
      "id": 488376,
      "primary_message": "Meanwhile, shave cilantro leaves off the stems; discard stems and mince the leaves.",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "id": 488377,
      "primary_message": "When the cauliflower rice is done, remove from heat, add cilantro, and stir to combine. ",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "id": 488378,
      "primary_message": "To serve, divide cauliflower rice and curry between plates or bowls. Enjoy! ",
      "secondary_message": null
    }
  ],
